<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patirruppattu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Patirruppattu is an anthology of classical Tamil poetry, one of the Eight Anthologies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sangam-literature">Sangam literature</a>. It originally contained ten sets of ten poems, each praising a Chera king; the first and last sets are lost. It is a main source for the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chera-dynasty">Chera dynasty</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imayavaramban-nedunceralatan">Imayavaramban Nedunceralatan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senguttuvan">Senguttuvan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patirruppattu.jpg" alt="Patirruppattu" width="320" height="533" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sengai Podhuvan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Book_Extract_Pathirrup_pathu.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
